*After 10 years, Yes after 10 years this scholarship by the Govt. of
Pakistan came back. It was last announced in 2016. *
Since then, HEC only offered it for Engineering & Technology in limited
fields in 2021 & 2022. Students from many other disciplines did not have
the same opportunity.Think about it: Many of the professors teaching you
today studied abroad on this very and similar scholarship of the Government

For the first time in a decade, *Social Sciences, Business & Governance*
and other non-engineering fields are back on the list. This is not a small
window =E2=80=94 this is a once-in-ten-years chance to fund your MS/M.Phil =
=E2=86=92 PhD
abroad, fully funded by the Government of Pakistan.
*Overseas Scholarship for MS/M.Phil & PhD Studies under Phase-III.*

*Eligible Fields (Phase-III):*

   - Digital Transformation & Emerging Technologies
   - Energy, Climate Change & Environment
   - Agriculture, Food Security & Agri-Tech
   - Health, Biotechnology & Life Sciences
   - Engineering & Advanced Manufacturing
   - Natural & Physical Sciences
   - Social Sciences, Business & Governance
   - Interdisciplinary & Strategic Fields

*What You Need to Do:*
1. Check if you already have a valid HAT score (valid for 2 years) =E2=80=
=94 if
not, register and take the *HEC Aptitude Test (HAT)*. Aim for your maximum
possible score =E2=80=94 it directly affects your merit.
2. Complete your online application for it on the HEC portal before the
deadline (28th August).
3. Review the full eligibility criteria, quotas, and required documents on
the official HEC page.

*Key Dates:*
Online application deadline: *28 August 2026, 4:00 PM*

*For HAT Test registration deadline, check online *

*For Details Visit:*

https://gradwinner.com/articles/hec-overseas-scholarship-2026
